# pins: wsp:member
# why: sh:pattern "^https?://|^did:" on wsp:member. A urn: member is an acceptance attributed to a party the other organisation cannot resolve, which is the same failure the file's header calls out for every other principal. It is also the case that only a second engine can check, because sh:pattern against an IRI is the constraint our engine used to skip.

